WEBVTT

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.480
Lancelot!

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.880
You can't go see the Mother Dragon if your leg's like that.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.580
Better just give up.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:33.760
As if I'd ever do that!

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.580
I need a Pal!

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.600
I didn't come all this way to turn back now!

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.190
I understand. So you need a Pal, huh?

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.240
Yeah.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.270
Then there's only one solution.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.950
I'll carry you, and we'll look for the Mother Dragon together!

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.950
<i>That was right after my seventh birthday,</i>

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:09.590
<i>the time of the Orphan's Rite, when the Mother Dragon</i>

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.700
<i>gifted humans with baby dragons.</i>

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.470
<i>I wonder what that boy is up to now.</i>

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.680
A dragon?

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.740
This looks like...

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.960
I can't remember.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.010
In between the Zepharos Empire to the north

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:51.240
and the Chevron Kingdom to the south

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.100
lies Lautreamont Knight Country.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.340
Known as "Dragon-Rearing Land,"

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:59.740
it boasts the largest dragon population on the Arc Strada continent.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.290
This small country with fewer than five million citizens

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.720
is home to a unique school:

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.140
Ansullivan Dragonar Academy.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.730
It aims to educate and guide dragon masters

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.840
and the so-called Breeders,
those young men and women

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.620
who have entered into bonds with dragons.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:06.050
Today we welcome three new members to the Student Council of Ansullivan Dragonar Academy.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:10.630
Allow me to introduce them to you.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.640
First, in charge of public morals: Silvia Lautreamont!

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.740
Thank you.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.740
I am Silvia Lautreamont, public morals officer.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.280
As a novice, I am sure I have my share of flaws,

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.910
but I shall endeavor to do my utmost.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.080
I look forward to serving.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:41.130
Next, our number-one problem child, in charge of general affairs:

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.500
Ash Blake!

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.890
Ash Blake, general affairs.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:05:02.330
To be honest... I'm not sure what I can bring to the table.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.060
H-However, I'll do my best regardless!

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.840
Thanks in advance!

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.980
You can do it, Ash!

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.040
Good luck!

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:30.800
And finally, a face familiar to all of you,

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.310
Ash Blake's Pal,

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.980
the humanoid dragon, Eco!

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:41.060
Let's give a warm welcome to our new school mascot!

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.820
Say hello, Eco.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:04.420
Rawr!

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:24.230
Wh-What's all this?

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:30.240
How irritating!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.140
It's a grave sin to make a laughingstock out of the proud dragon race!

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:38.500
Stupid, dummy dum-dum humans!

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.360
Cosette was being thoughtful, in her way.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.630
Besides, no one was making fun of you. Trust me.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:45.740
Huh?

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:49.940
They saw how interesting you are and felt a bond with you.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:52.010
Is that a good thing?

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:57.020
Sure it is! That means everyone wants to be your friend.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:01.950
Hm... Then I'd be happy to make them all my servants.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:02.980
Now listen here...

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:09.660
So...

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.820
this is your first job as a Student Council member?

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:17.760
Yeah. I'm supposed to take down anything posted without permission.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:22.380
Just remember who your master is.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.700
Don't go letting anyone else boss you around, you hear me?!

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:27.300
Actually, I'm <i>your</i> master.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:32.300
"Silver Knight Fan Club"?

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.810
Who's this Silver Knight, anyway?

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:40.100
He's the hero from a popular novel, "The Heavenly Dragonar."

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.720
They say he got his name because he resembled the Archdragonar

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.310
who saved the town from Necromancia.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.560
So wait. Isn't this <i>your</i> fan club?

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.600
I guess you could say that.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:02.580
Watch where you're aiming!

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.340
I'm runnin' out of ammo!

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:07.580
It's her!

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.880
The Iron Blood Valkyrie!

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:14.340
Fire!

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:18.700
Little embers like you,

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.850
if left to burn,

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:24.600
can grow to engulf an entire nation!

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.340
Study hall, huh?

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.760
Hey, Eco!

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.750
You looked so adorable in that dress.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:52.750
Say, Ash, wanna swap-

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.720
He had that coming.

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:12.260
Greetings. I am first-year Senios Jessica Valentine,

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:16.980
president of the Silver Knight Fan Club, or SKFC for short.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:22.620
And I'm the SKFC vice-president, first-year Junios Lynette Worth.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:29.260
We have not met the Silver Knight, the object of our admiration.

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:31.960
Therefore, we are seeking information.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:37.860
Did anyone here see the hero who vanquished the Necromancia?

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:41.470
We're in the middle of class now. Please leave.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:46.020
My, my. If it isn't the princess.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.120
Not now it isn't.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.020
I'm warning you as the Student Council's public morals officer.

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:55.910
Public morals? How very trivial!

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:58.510
Why, that pales in comparison to my ambition!

00:09:58.510 --> 00:09:59.800
What ambition?

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:02.910
Allow me to elucidate.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.860
My ambition...

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:05.910
is to...

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:11.670
bear the Silver Knight's children!

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.430
Miss President!

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:28.180
That statement is in violation of SKFC statute 127 and our motto:

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.940
"Pure, True, Lovely"!

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:35.480
That's our vice president for you.
Nice catch, Lynette.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.700
I hereby retract that statement.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.950
Retraction acknowledged.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.140
Why so by-the-book?

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:45.900
Resistance is useless and could be painful.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:48.960
She's from a long and distinguished line of nobility.

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:50.570
In point of fact...

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:51.790
Mm-hmm.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:55.620
What's that? The princess was present at the Necromancia incident?!

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:57.680
Mm-hmm.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:00.840
And riding Lancelot at that.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:05.720
So perhaps <i>you</i> know the Silver Knight's secret identity.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.600
D-Don't be ridiculous!

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:14.300
Hey, listen!

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.320
We're in the middle of class here.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.110
Would you leave?

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:24.370
To think a mere commoner would speak his mind to me, of all people!

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:29.870
Acting the fool again,

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:31.700
Jessica?

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:35.000
Rebecca! Can I help you?

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:39.880
I have business with the Student Council members.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:44.890
Perfect. As president of the SKFC,

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:50.180
I demand that the Student Council disclose its information on the Necromancia incident.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:03.940
Y-You may have won <i>this</i> battle,

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:05.340
but I'll win the war!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:28.260
So Jessica isn't nobility?

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:29.760
That's right.

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:34.390
Her family's been in service to us Randalls for generations.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:39.780
So when she starts making trouble, I threaten to expose her.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:43.530
But why the ruse?

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:49.050
Jessica's a good person, but between her dreamy personality

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:51.420
and her admiration for royalty and nobility,

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:54.560
apparently she's come to believe that she herself is high-born.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.540
The things we talk ourselves into.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:02.430
But if she finds the Silver Knight, she really <i>can</i> become a noble.

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:03.880
What do you mean?

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:08.380
In this dragon-rearing country of ours,

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:11.160
Arch corresponds to a noble rank.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:14.600
If she marries the Arch-bearing Silver Knight,

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.760
her future would be all but guaranteed.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:21.920
If she finds out the Silver Knight is really you, Ash Blake,

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.700
Jessica will set her sights on your essence for sure.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.700
E-Essence?!

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.420
What's that? Is it yummy?

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.950
You do <i>not</i> need to know!

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:36.810
But if you know, it's only fair that I know too.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:38.170
What kind of logic is that?

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:42.380
Hmph! I have a little something called the Draguarth.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.480
E-Essence?!

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:59.830
In any case... Ash, you must take care to keep your identity under wraps.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:02.230
Jessica is a very tenacious girl.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.240
Understood.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.760
Now on to our main topic.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:16.300
As it happens, First Princess Veronica Lautreamont

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:20.250
will be paying a visit to the town of Ansullivan in the wake of the Necromancia attack.

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:24.660
A sympathy call from First Princess Veronica?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:26.420
That's serious business.

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.010
First Princess. That must mean...

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:32.560
Yes. She's Silvia's big sister.

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:34.520
No!

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:55.940
Setting course for Ansullivan.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:57.290
Roger.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.800
We'll be seeing her soon, Glen.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:01.790
Indeed.

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:06.560
I'm so looking forward to it. My little sister, Silvia.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:14.540
M-My elder sister-that <i>tyrant</i>-
here, in Ansullivan?

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.920
Bye now!

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.600
Beautiful flowers for sale!

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:31.070
<i>Master Milgauss told me to learn more about the boy who killed the Necromancia,</i>

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.660
<i>but he's not that easy to find.</i>

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:03.680
What's gotten into the princess, anyway?

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:06.160
Must be Veronica's impending visit.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:09.460
She's been like this ever since she heard the news.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:10.610
Well, then...

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:13.740
should I explain?

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.160
Cosette!

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:21.370
Are you concerned about the reasons behind her state of shock as a classmate?

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.900
Or as a man?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:26.020
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:30.760
We've fought together, and we're both Student Council members.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.880
It's only natural that I'd be worried.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:36.240
Then let's leave it at that.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:42.280
Even though Veronica wasn't selected as a Breeder,

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:48.020
she rebelled against that rejection by strengthening her body and perfecting her sword skills.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.220
Soon she earned herself another name.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.240
The Iron Blood Valkyrie.

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:58.960
Her personality was so intense that she put her young sister through various drills,

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:02.010
all "for her own good."

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:04.040
Drills... Now <i>that's</i> an exaggeration.

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:08.000
Not at all.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.550
Those were brutal days.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.780
Survival exercises in the mountains...

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.900
If you want to live, cut a path for yourself.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.140
Pick up that sword.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:45.980
And so Veronica has become a symbol of terror for the princess.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.160
How traumatic.

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.170
No wonder she's afraid of her.

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:56.170
Princess?

00:17:58.150 --> 00:17:59.420
Princess!

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:05.180
Um, if you like, you could come to me for advice.

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:10.000
I, uh, I don't really know how I could help, but...

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.940
Look how far I've fallen.

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:12.690
Huh?

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:15.070
To think <i>you</i> would pity <i>me</i> !

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.460
Save your concern.

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:23.700
Geez. I go out of my way and...

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.160
She's just putting on a brave face.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:38.200
Tomorrow, huh?

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.800
The scent is wonderful.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.890
It's lavender.

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:02.410
It has the effect of easing mental stress.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.740
Mental stress?

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:15.720
You haven't been sleeping well for the past few days.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:16.880
So you knew.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.890
This should help you get a good night's sleep.

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:28.270
Y-You don't have to apply it there.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.610
Oh, excuse me.

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:31.270
Then...

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.820
That tickles!

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:37.280
Oh, excuse me, again.

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:39.280
Now...

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:42.030
S-Stop that.

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:45.530
Hey, enough of that!

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:48.040
Cosette!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:52.540
I haven't seen you laugh in a long time.

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:56.010
Cosette...

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:03.560
Good night.

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.060
Then there's only one solution.

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:25.720
I'll carry you, and we'll look for the Mother Dragon together!

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:30.120
Okay, here we go.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:36.250
<i>I made... that boy a promise.</i>

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:39.710
<i>That I'd be a fine, upstanding knight.</i>

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:53.220
Behave yourself around Princess Veronica, Eco.

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:56.740
And you behave yourself around me.

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:58.680
I don't want a big scene, all right?

00:20:58.680 --> 00:21:01.180
Just be a good girl, and I'll buy you a crepe.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:04.400
You will?! Then I suppose I'll do what you say!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.590
Where's the princess?

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:12.320
I couldn't force her to come,
not when she's that terrified.

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:13.790
You're right.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:17.000
Still, to be that scared of your own sister...

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.420
Who's scared of whom now?

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:22.920
Princess!

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.620
Greetings.

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.060
Are you all right?

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:34.030
To whom do you think you're speaking?

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:37.340
I am Silvia Lautreamont.

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:40.980
You may have seen me in a rather unbecoming moment,

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:42.020
but I'm fine now.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:44.780
I see. Well, that's good.

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:47.280
Here she comes.

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:05.030
Oh ho! That's First Princess Veronica's-

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:08.300
It looks like an Imperial airship.

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:13.120
That's Princess Veronica's personal vehicle, the Magiship <i>Sylvanus</i>.

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:15.310
How does a thing like that even fly?

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:20.000
It runs on a special kind of Fafnirite called Millennium.

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:21.820
A special kind of Fafnirite?

00:22:22.790 --> 00:22:28.320
Thousand-year-old dragon fossils turn into mana-rich crystals.

00:22:28.770 --> 00:22:31.400
So that's Millennium.

00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:46.540
Princess Veronica has come into view!

00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:04.860
So that's...

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:12.180
Veronica Lautreamont, First Princess.

00:25:00.810 --> 00:25:01.370
That's a lot!

00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:02.880
And I now will list them all!

00:25:02.880 --> 00:25:03.630
Oh, no, you don't!

00:25:03.630 --> 00:25:04.030
One.

00:25:04.030 --> 00:25:05.480
Stop!
